          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: طبیعت",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "طبیعت (tabi'at) — \"nature\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ما جمعه ها به دل طبیعت میرویم. Mâ jom'e-hâ be del-e tabi'at miravim. On Fridays we go out into the countryside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Del-e tabi'at — the heart of nature, out in the wild."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tabi'at was borrowed from Arabic ṭabīʿa 'nature, natural disposition' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
