          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حفاظت کردن (hefâzat kardan) — \"to protect, to conserve\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مردم روستا از جنگل حفاظت میکنند. Mardom-e rustâ az jangal hefâzat mikonand. The villagers protect the forest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The thing protected takes az. Mantaqe-ye hefâzat-shode — a protected area."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hefâzat kardan is built from hefâzat 'protection', borrowed from Arabic ḥifāẓa, which EtymDB derives from ḥafiẓa 'to guard, to know by heart', the source of hefz kardan 'to keep, to memorize', and kardan 'to do'."
            }
          ]
        },
